        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0628" n="1588" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1588"/>

                <head>No. 1082.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Straus.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 17,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 71 of the 30th
                    ultimo, in which the Ottoman Government requests you to instruct the consul of
                    the United States at Odessa not to interpose objection to the return to Turkey
                    of H. A. Proios, whose extradition is demanded from Russia.</p>
                <p>Mr. Thomas E. Heenan, the consul, has been called upon for full information in
                    regard to the case.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
